{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-019", "content_sha256": "0dea73f5654ce880bc727337c3942b76e65f7d4bd7640c804b9dbe1e00add444", "heading": "MS-019", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-019", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-019", "text": "### MS-019 — ALLOW: permitted variants of the required answer\n\n**Claim:** ALLOW grants variants of the same underlying answer, including partial\ndescriptions.\n**Evidence:** \"ALLOW black / ALLOW any combination of grey and black eg grey-black\"\non the colour-completion task (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 60-74).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-020", "content_sha256": "8eb2cabb280941f7e99ae776765e4eb2e643f991a71c0daed0410c3c3a1d8166", "heading": "MS-020", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-020", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-020", "text": "### MS-020 — ACCEPT: equivalent responses to method points\n\n**Claim:** ACCEPT admits an equivalent formulation of a method or action point.\n**Evidence:** \"M1 add chlorine (solution) to potassium bromide ACCEPT mix the two\n(solutions) solutions\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 96-110).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-021", "content_sha256": "6ab31d956546753d318304d2314084867aa44d651881bb71281ca8a9ba1c8c34", "heading": "MS-021", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-021", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-021", "text": "### MS-021 — Observation and product-form alternatives\n\n**Claim:** observation and product statements accept alternative phrasings printed\ninline.\n**Evidence:** \"M2 (solution) turns orange ALLOW any combination of\norange/yellow/brown\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 96-110);\nthe parsed excerpt\n(SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 98-112).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-022", "content_sha256": "502797ec8e06aea8e500810b4f92d449e7bb6c807f7b66d1b1f5fd966b32474c", "heading": "MS-022", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-022", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-022", "text": "### MS-022 — Reverse-argument acceptance\n\n**Claim:** some conclusion points explicitly accept the inverse reasoning route.\n**Evidence:** \"M4 (therefore) chlorine is more reactive (than bromine) ACCEPT\nreverse argument\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 110-124).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-023", "content_sha256": "95aaae09ef62b08598f5d32b3033005c6b8ab34af1e2703031dd61307e077d9e", "heading": "MS-023", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-023", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-023", "text": "### MS-023 — Name/symbol pairs as printed alternatives\n\n**Claim:** chemical names and formulae are printed as interchangeable pairs in both\nanswers and allowances.\n**Evidence:** \"bromine/Br2\" across the displacement scheme's points (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 116-130); the noble-gas pair \"argon and helium\nALLOW Ar and He\" on the 2CR atmosphere item .\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-024", "content_sha256": "b4012e2fba6c47038a32c60634e3a662ff085fa8268a245140b3f4680e50cf84", "heading": "MS-024", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-024", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-024", "text": "### MS-024 — Alternative scoring routes\n\n**Claim:** a point can name a second route by which it may be earned.\n**Evidence:** \"M3 can be scored by Br2 as a product in an equation\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 110-124).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
